# The userscript is a build artifact that CI rebuilds and byte-compares against
# the committed copy. That comparison only means anything if the build is
# reproducible, and it is not reproducible while line endings depend on which OS
# checked the sources out: a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true hands
# build.mjs CRLF sources and it embeds those carriage returns in the bundle,
# while Linux CI reads LF and produces a different file from the same commit.
#
# Normalizing to LF in the working tree -- not just in the index -- is what makes
# `node build.mjs` produce identical bytes everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish and generated content that must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
